+# AGENTS.md — NC Manager V1.21
+
+Compact guidance for OpenCode / AI agents working in this repo. Read it first; it captures the non-obvious facts that cost the most time to re-learn.
+
+## Commands
+
+```bash
+# Run the GUI (from repo root)
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m nccorrection.main
+# Smoke-test mode (no GUI window) — good for headless/CI
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m nccorrection.main --no-gui
+# Full test suite (unittest)
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -q
+# One test / one class
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest tests.test_ui.TestUI.test_confirm_close_clean_quits_directly
+```
+
+- `rg` (ripgrep) is **not** installed here. Use the Grep tool or `grep -RIn`.
+- Qt test modules set `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` themselves, so headless runs from the repo root with `PYTHONPATH=src` just work.
+- Python 3.12+. Pinned deps in `requirements.lock.txt` (PySide6 6.11.1, ezdxf 1.4.4).
+
+## Architecture (what the filenames don't tell you)
+
+- Package root is `src/nccorrection/`. Subpackages: `core/` (NC parsing, classification, geometry, `viewer`), `ui/` (Qt app + 2D/3D/blueprint viewers, themes, `translations`), `services/` (project/settings/audit/resource persistence), `engine/` (DSTV parsers, `dxf/` isolated reader, steel `catalog`, `render_2d`).
+- **Canonical geometry contract**: `core/viewer.parse_geometry(text)` returns a geometry dict; hole edits go through `core/hole_ops.apply_edits(geometry, overrides, deleted, added)`. The DXF reader (`engine/dxf/dxf_parser.py`) emits the *same* dict on purpose, so the 2D viewer renders DXF with zero engine changes — treat `parse_geometry`'s dict shape as the integration boundary; don't fork viewers per format.
+- **`ui/app.py` → `NCManagerApp`** is the central application object (large). Persistence/import logic lives in `services/project_service.py`. UI calls services; keep that direction.
+- **Close confirmation** (`_confirm_close`) opens only when there are unsaved edits OR files added in the current session (`_session_added`). A session that imported but did nothing else still prompts (ProNest-style); a truly idle session closes silently.
+
+## Hard constraints (easy to violate, costly to fix)
+
+- **Never modify the user's original source files.** The app works on imported *copies* (`shutil.copy2` into `projects/<name>/`). "Original" save mode writes in place only on an explicit user Save-Original action; everything else is a copy.
+- **Storage paths shown to the user use the original file name — never a hash.** Flat storage is the rule (owner law 2026-08-19); legacy `input/<hash>.nc1` paths are kept only until an explicit migration. Don't reintroduce hash-based paths.
+- **Do not delete code that "looks unused."** Several members are intentionally retained (e.g. `_scan_folder`, `_popup_cancel_menu`). If you suspect dead code, grep/refcheck first and confirm removal with the owner before touching it.
+- **Do not add or replace dependencies without explicit owner approval.** ezdxf was added deliberately (MIT, isolated engine); numpy is deliberately *not* used.
+- **Do not commit unless the owner explicitly orders it.** When you do, write a detailed message.
+
+## Testing gotchas
+
+- `tests/test_ui.py::test_default_columns_primary` **currently FAILS** — known pre-existing issue (column-order expectation), fails on the pre-session tree too, unrelated to recent work. Do not "fix" it without owner direction.
+- Flaky in a full run but pass alone: `test_ask_save_copy`, `test_animated_button_hover_animates`. If the full suite shows one failing, re-run it in isolation before assuming a regression.
+- Current baseline: ~611 tests, 610 OK + the one known failure above (~37s).
+- Full E2E harness (52 real operations, currently 52/52) lives in `tools/e2e_walkthrough.py`. Run headless from the repo root:
+  `PYTHONPATH=src QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen python tools/e2e_walkthrough.py`
+
+## DXF / DWG specifics
+
+- **DXF import is 2D only** — it always yields a PLATE profile, never a 3D body.
+- **DWG needs an external converter** (ODA File Converter in `Program Files\ODA\ODAFileConverter`, or the LibreDWG route). If none is configured, the user gets a clear message and **nothing is modified** — never block or silently guess.
+
+## Where to look next
+
+- `PROJECT_STATE.md` (repo root): current state, append-only decisions log, confirmed-working features, open questions. Read it at the start of every session.
+- Governance / global rules: `C:\Users\ouahb\Desktop\brain code V2.2\AGENTS.md` and `C:\Users\ouahb\Desktop\brain code V2.2\opencodeقواعد_البناء\00_INDEX.md`. Read the `core/` rules and `industrial/industrial_programming_rules.md` before any NC Manager implementation.
+- Module detail: `docs/architecture/*.md`.
+
+## Python protocol for NC Manager
+
+- This is a Python 3.12+ / PySide6 / `unittest` application, not the .NET OptiNest codebase. Apply the Brain's governance, evidence, anti-duplication, and industrial-safety rules; do not run its OptiNest-specific `dotnet` baseline commands here.
+- Baseline for this repository is `PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -q`, followed by the headless E2E walkthrough when a change affects a user workflow.
+- Before changing code, inspect `PROJECT_STATE.md`, identify the exact module boundary, search for an existing equivalent, and record the command results and any deviation from the requested scope.
+- For CNC, geometry, import/export, storage, or file-writing changes, preserve originals, validate the mathematical result and boundary cases, and never claim production readiness without the relevant automated evidence.
