+---
+
+## 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
+
+| Feature | Engine Status | UI Status | What's Missing |
+|---------|-------------|-----------|----------------|
+| AdvancedProfileCreator | **COMPLETE** | **MISSING** (wiring only) | Widget that wires all existing engines into one CAD-like UI |
+| Dimension Tools Panel | **COMPLETE** (7 types, renderer, detector, geometry) | **MISSING** (no toolbar widget) | Dropdown toolbar exposing dimension tools to user |
+
+**Key finding:** Both features have 100% of their engine/math/rendering code already built. What's missing is the **UI glue** — widgets that wire the engines together and expose them in the toolbar.
+
+---
+
+## 2. FEATURE 1: AdvancedProfileCreator
+
+### 2.1 What It Is
+
+A CAD-like widget (QMainWindow) that combines:
+- Left panel: Profile catalog + parameters (profile, length, angles, material)
+- Center: Live 2D/3D canvas (existing NcViewer)
+- Right panel: Holes/slots table + dimension tools
+- Top: Ribbon toolbar (File, Edit, Draw, Modify, Dim, Annotate)
+
+**This replaces the current `CreatePartDialog`** — which is a basic QDialog with a simple splitter layout. The AdvancedProfileCreator would be a full MainWindow with all engines wired.
+
+### 2.2 Existing Engines (ALL COMPLETE)
+
+#### Contour Engine (`engine/contour/`)
+```
+engine/contour/
+├── __init__.py              ← Public API (115 lines)
+├── contour_builder.py       ← Phase 3-4: builds face contours (164 lines)
+├── profile_model.py         ← ProfileGeometryModel (288 lines)
+├── cut_interpreter.py       ← Trapezoidal cuts (160 lines)
+├── notch_detector.py        ← W/T suffix detection (118 lines)
+├── nc1_writer_advanced.py   ← Full NC1 output (153 lines)
+├── builders/                ← Modern: face/segment/closure builders
+├── interpreters/            ← Modern: web/flange cut interpreters
+├── detectors/               ← Modern: notch/suffix detectors
+├── writers/                 ← Modern: NC1 writer + formatter
+├── validators/              ← Closure validator
+├── geometry/                ← Dimensions, Point2D, Vector2D
+├── core/                    ← Enums, constants, exceptions
+├── models/                  ← ProfileGeometryModel, CutAngles, etc.
+└── registry/                ← Face configuration registry
+```
+
+**API entry points:**
+- `generate_nc1(dims, kind_code, ...)` → NC1 text string
+- `create_profile_model(st_line, ak_lines)` → ProfileGeometryModel
+- `ContourBuilder.build_all_faces(model)` → list of ContourFace
+- `NC1WriterAdvanced.write_nc1(model)` → NC1 text string
+
+#### DXF Reader (`engine/dxf/`)
+```
+engine/dxf/
+├── __init__.py
+└── dxf_parser.py            ← Full DXF reader (448 lines)
+```
+
+**API entry point:**
+- `read_dxf(path=None, text=None, thickness, profile)` → geometry dict (same contract as `parse_geometry`)
+
+#### Profile Catalog (`engine/steel_engine/catalog.py`)
+- 200+ profiles: IPE, HEA, HEB, HEM, UPN, UPE, L-angles, tubes, bars, plates
+- EN 10365 verified data
+- `SteelProfile` dataclass with Mémotech fields
+
+**API:**
+- `has_profile(name)` → bool
+- `get_profile(name)` → SteelProfile
+- `profile_names()` → list of str
+- `iter_profiles()` → iterator
+
+#### Snap Engine (`engine/math/osnap.py`)
+- 8 snap kinds: ENDPOINT, MIDPOINT, NEAREST, INTERSECTION, CENTRE, TANGENT, EXTENSION, INSERTION
+- Polar tracking
+- `OsnapTargets` dataclass
+- Facade: `design/snaps.py`
+
+#### Dimensioning Engine (`design/dimensioning/`)
+- 7 dimension types (see Feature 2 section below)
+- Auto-detect circles + bolt circles
+- QPainter renderer
+
+#### Profile Catalog NC1 Writer (`engine/profile_catalog/nc1_writer.py`)
+- `generate_beam_nc1()` — used by CreatePartDialog
+- 37 NC1 template files in `templates/`
+
+### 2.3 Existing UI Components
+
+| Component | File | Status | What It Does |
