+## 3. FEATURE 2: Dimension Tools Panel
+
+### 3.1 What It Is
+
+A dropdown toolbar button (or panel) that exposes 6 dimension tools:
+1. **Linear** — horizontal/vertical dimension between two points
+2. **Aligned** — parallel-to-edge dimension
+3. **Angular** — angle between two lines
+4. **Radius** — leader line to circle/arc edge
+5. **Diameter** — line through circle center with two arrows
+6. **Leader** — text note with arrow
+
+Plus an **Auto-detect** mode that uses the existing `auto_dimensions()`.
+
+### 3.2 Existing Engine (ALL COMPLETE)
+
+#### `design/dimensioning/types.py` (337 lines)
+```
+Enums:
+  DimType        → RADIUS, DIAMETER, ANGULAR, LINEAR, LEADER, CENTER_MARK
+  ArrowStyle     → FILLED, OPEN, TICK, DOT, NONE
+  TextPlacement  → OUTSIDE, INSIDE, ALONG, HORIZONTAL, ABOVE
+  LeaderStyle    → STRAIGHT, BENT, SPLINE
+
+Data types:
+  Point2D(x, y)           → distance_to(), angle_to(), lerp(), offset(), rotated()
+  Circle(center, radius)  → contains_point()
+  Arc(center, radius, start, end) → point_at(), sweep_deg
+
+Dimension entities:
+  RadiusDimension(center, point_on_circle, radius, angle_deg, label, text_placement, face)
+  DiameterDimension(center, point_on_circle, diameter, angle_deg, label, text_placement, face)
+  AngularDimension(vertex, line1_end, line2_end, dim_arc_radius, label, text_placement, face)
+  LinearDimension(point1, point2, offset, angle_deg, label, text_placement, face)
+  LeaderDimension(start, tail, text, face)
+  CenterMark(center, mark_size, extended, radius, face)
+  BoltCirclePattern(center, bolt_radius, hole_positions, hole_diameter, face)
+
+Container:
+  DimensionGroup(face, radii, diameters, angulars, linears, leaders, center_marks, bolt_circles)
+```
+
+#### `design/dimensioning/renderer.py` (501 lines)
+```
+class DimensionRenderer(painter, style, to_screen):
+  draw_radius(dim)        → center→edge line + arrow + tail + text
+  draw_diameter(dim)      → diameter line + two arrows + tail + text
+  draw_angular(dim)       → angle arc + extension lines + text
+  draw_linear(dim)        → dimension line + arrows + extension lines + text
+  draw_leader(dim)        → arrow + text note
+  draw_center_mark(cm)    → cross + optional extended dashes
+  draw_bolt_circle(bc)    → center mark + radius leader + angular spacing + Nx label
+  draw_group(group)       → batch draws all dimensions
+```
+
+#### `design/dimensioning/detector.py` (180 lines)
+```
+detect_circular_contours(geometry)  → [{center, radius, face, is_outer, contour_index}]
+detect_holes_on_circle(holes, tol) → [BoltCirclePattern]
+auto_dimensions(geometry)           → DimensionGroup  ← MAIN ENTRY POINT
+```
+
+#### `design/dimensioning/geometry.py` (352 lines)
+```
+circle_from_3_points(p1, p2, p3)           → Circle
+circle_center_from_contour(pts)            → Point2D
+circle_radius_from_contour(pts, center)    → float
+arc_points(center, radius, start, end, n)  → [Point2D]
+leader_endpoint(center, point, length)     → Point2D
+text_position_for_radius(...)              → Point2D
+text_position_for_diameter(...)            → Point2D
+text_position_for_angular(...)             → Point2D
+detect_bolt_circles(positions, tol, min)   → [BoltCirclePattern]
+angular_spacing(positions, center)         → float
+```
+
+#### `design/dimensioning/style.py` (195 lines)
+```
+DimensionStyle       → 35+ visual properties
+DEFAULT_STYLE        → dark theme (amber on dark)
+BLUEPRINT_STYLE      → light theme (blue on white)
+style_from_theme(theme) → adapted style
+```
+
+### 3.3 Current Integration
+
+The dimension engine is already wired into the 2D viewer:
+
+```python
+# qt_viewer_painting.py line 548-561
+def _draw_contour_radius_label(self, p):
+    from nccorrection.design.dimensioning import (
+        DimensionRenderer, auto_dimensions, style_from_theme)
+    dims = auto_dimensions(self._geometry)     # auto-detect
+    if dims.is_empty:
+        return
+    style = style_from_theme(self._mp)
+    renderer = DimensionRenderer(p, style, self._to_screen)
+    renderer.draw_group(dims)
+```
+
+This is called from `_draw_cotation()` when `self._cotation` is True.
+
+### 3.4 What's Missing
+
+| Component | Status | What's Needed |
+|-----------|--------|---------------|
+| Dimension toolbar widget | **MISSING** | New `DimensionToolbar(QWidget)` in `ui/toolbars/` |
+| Tool selection state | **MISSING** | Active tool tracking (which dim type is selected) |
+| Click-to-dimension | **MISSING** | User clicks 2 points → dimension appears |
+| Interactive preview | **MISSING** | Rubber-band line during point selection |
+| Undo support | **MISSING** | Dimension add = undoable operation |
+| Dimension storage | **MISSING** | Store dimensions per part in manifest |
+| Blueprint integration | **PARTIAL** | `_draw_contour_radius_label` works, but no user-placed dims |
+
+### 3.5 Approach Options
+
+**Option A: Toolbar dropdown only (Minimal)**
+- Add a "Dim" button to the main toolbar
+- Dropdown: Linear / Aligned / Angular / Radius / Diameter / Leader / Auto
+- Auto mode = existing `auto_dimensions()`
+- Manual modes = click 2 points → dimension placed
+- Risk: Simple but limited
+
+**Option B: Toolbar + interactive canvas (Full)**
+- Option A + rubber-band preview during point selection
+- Click first point → rubber-band follows cursor → click second point → dimension placed
+- Dimension stored in `geometry['user_dimensions']` list
+- Undo/redo for dimension operations
+- Risk: More complex, but uses existing renderer
+
+**Option C: Floating panel (Advanced)**
+- Option B + floating dock widget with dimension properties
+- Style editor (arrow style, text size, color)
+- Layer management (show/hide dimension types)
+- Risk: Over-engineered for current needs
+
+**Recommended: Option A** — start with dropdown + auto-detect, add interactive later.
