+## 3. SUPPORTED FILE FORMATS
+
+| Format | Read | Write | Engine | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------|--------|-------|
+| NC1 / DSTV | ✅ | ✅ | `engine/parser/dstv_parser.py` (DstvParser) + `core/nc1_tools.py`, `core/nc1_writer.py` | ST header (12 dims incl. weight-per-m `dims[6]`), AK/IK contour blocks, BO holes, suffix letters ('s' start-end ref, 'w' notch, 'u'/'o' flange-edge cut). Face semantics: v=web, o=top flange, u=bottom flange, h=rear web. |
+| NC (`.nc`) | ✅ | ✅ | same as NC1 | treated as NC1-family; same parser. |
+| DXF (R12+ ASCII/binary) | ✅ | ✅ | read: `engine/dxf/dxf_parser.py` (ezdxf 1.4.4); write: `core/dxf_writer.py` | **DXF import is 2D only — always yields a PLATE profile, never a 3D body.** Inner closed contours = holes. |
+| DWG | ⚠️ planned | ❌ | none (external converter only) | Needs ODA File Converter or LibreDWG `dwg2dxf.exe` via subprocess. If none configured → clear message, **nothing modified**. |
+| OBJ / STL | ❌ | ✅ | `core/part3d.py` (3D model) | 3D export of the built part. |
+| PDF | ❌ | ✅ | `ui/pdf_export.py` | Paints a widget into a PDF. |
+| CN | ❌ | ✅ | `core/nc1_writer.py` family | machining-text export. |
+
+**Geometry contract (the integration boundary):** `core/viewer.parse_geometry(text)` returns a geometry dict; hole edits go through `core/hole_ops.apply_edits(...)`. The DXF reader emits the **same dict shape on purpose**, so the 2D viewer renders DXF with zero engine changes. The 3D part model is built in `core/part3d.py` from the same geometry.
