+## 10. NC PARSER (NC1/DSTV)
+
+Located in `engine/parser/dstv_parser.py` (`DstvParser`) + `engine/parser/dstv_part.py` (`DstvPart`) + `engine/parser/dstv_face.py` (`DstvFace`). The app-level geometry contract (dict) comes from `core/viewer.py` `parse_geometry`.
+
+**ST header** — 12 dimension slots. `dims[6]` = weight per metre (kg/m). Fields extracted: mark, profile, type letter, material, length, dimensions.
+
+**Contours** — `AK` (primary), `IK` (secondary) blocks define the part outline per face.
+
+**Holes** — `BO` block: lines `face x y d` (round) and slot forms; `is_slot` determines slot width/length/angle. A hole line MUST precede `EN` for the parser to see it.
+
+**Suffix letters** — `s` (start-end reference), `w` (notch), `u` / `o` (flange-edge cut).
+
+**Face semantics (DSTV standard, verified against real Lantek + DSTV):**
+- `v` = web (vertical leg)
+- `o` = top flange
+- `u` = bottom flange
+- `h` = rear web
+
+**L-profile (angle) mapping (locked):** `v` → vertical leg b (normal (0,1,0)); `u` → horizontal leg a (normal (0,0,-1)).
+
+**Classification (`core/classifier.py`):**
+- Structural ST-block extraction (`_extract_st_profile`): locate ST → terminator codes (`AK/IK/BO/SI/PU/KO/KA/EN`) → profile-type letter line → walk backward to nearest word-like line (skip `**`), = profile name.
+- **Strict PL/PLATE rule (CTO 2026-08-26):** bare `P` is invalid — valid plates are ALWAYS `PL`/`PLATE`-prefixed. A solitary `P` assembly mark (e.g. `P17`) is NEVER a plate. Bare-P legacy NC1 files now classify as UNKNOWN (intended, awaiting CTO acceptance of this deviation for production).
+- `DEFAULT` operates defensively — parsing/classification never raises.
+
+**Format analyzer (`engine/format_analyzer.py`):**
+- `detect_format(filepath)` → `'NC1' | 'DXF' | 'UNKNOWN'` (content-first). NC1 = standalone `ST` line + ≥1 data-block code. DXF = ASCII `0 SECTION 2 HEADER` / headerless `0 ENTITIES` / `AutoCAD Binary DXF` magic. Extension is only a fallback hint.
+- `analyze_file(filepath)` → `DetailReport` (format, profile_type, profile_name, material, thickness/width/length, holes_count, slots_count, faces_used, entity_counts, total_entities, warning, summary). Never raises.
+- DXF path is sniffer-only (entity counts + PLATE convention); holes/slots/dims need the full geometry parser (`read_dxf`).
+
+---
+
+## 11. DXF/DWG READINESS
+
+### DXF (READY)
+- `engine/dxf/dxf_parser.py` (ezdxf 1.4.4, isolated): R12+ ASCII/binary; LWPOLYLINE/POLYLINE (bulge-aware arc flattening), ARC, CIRCLE, LINE (endpoint chaining into loops), SPLINE/ELLIPSE (flattening); `$INSUNITS` → mm.
+- Largest closed loop = plate outline; contained loops = holes (area-equivalent Ø + centroid); multiple separate plates = multiple outers.
+- Emits the **same geometry-dict contract** as `parse_geometry` → 2D viewer renders with zero engine changes.
+- **DXF import is 2D only; always a PLATE profile; never a 3D body.**
+
+### DXF export (READY)
+- `core/dxf_writer.py` `export_dxf(geometry, path, scale, faces, layout)`. Legacy `faces=None` = OUTLINE/HOLES layers, byte-identical to before. Face mode = FACE_V/O/U/H layers, blueprint layout option.
+
+### DWG (NOT READY — blocked)
