+## 23. DIAGRAMS
+
+### 23.1 Layer diagram
+See §4 (text diagram). Layers: UI (PySide6) → Services → Core/Engine (pure Python).
+
+### 23.2 Data flow (single-file lifecycle)
+```
+source file → import (copy) → projects/<order>/<orig name> → classify → manifest
+   → parse_geometry → apply_hole_edits → 2D/3D/blueprint render
+   → save/open project → export (NC1/CN/DXF/OBJ/STL/PDF)
+   → dirty → close dialog → Save all | Cancel | Close without save
+```
+
+### 23.3 Geometry contract
+```
+parse_geometry(text) ──► dict {
+    profile, category, family, dims[], length, weight,
+    faces, contours, holes[ {face,x,y,d,is_slot,slot_length,slot_width,angle} ], ...
+}
+apply_edits(dict, overrides, deleted, added) ──► updated dict
+        │
+        ├──► 2D viewer         (NcViewer)
+        ├──► 3D viewer         (NcViewer3D via part3d)
+        └──► blueprint         (DstvRenderer2D)
+        └──► export engines    (nc1_writer / dxf_writer / OBJ / STL / PDF)
+```
+The DXF reader feeds the SAME dict → all viewers/exporters work on DXF with zero engine changes.
