+
+**Date:** 2026-09-11
+**Auditor role:** Guardian / Inspector (Zero-Trust protocol)
+**Method:** Read-only forensic scan — no application code was modified by this audit. Every claim below was verified against the working tree (file:line references). Some conclusions contradict earlier documentation (AGENTS.md / PROJECT_STATE.md) because the working tree has evolved; where the docs are stale, it is flagged explicitly.
+**Baseline (fresh, this audit):** `675/675 tests PASS` (workaround runner excluding the pre-existing-hang module `test_measure_global`), `0 failures`, `0 errors`, 42.8s. HEAD-known-failure `test_default_columns_primary` now PASSES in the working tree (fixed by an uncommitted `services/settings_service.py` change — see §5).
+
+---
+
+## 1. THE COMPLETED FOUNDATION (What We Built)
+
+Verified-integrated engineering milestones (code + tests + UI wiring):
+
+| # | Milestone | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **DSTV/NC1 parse engine** — ST header, AK/IK contours, BO holes/slots (incl. angular slots + `l` marker), bevels, notches, bulge arcs, SI/EN | `core/viewer.py` (618 l), `engine/parser/dstv_parser.py` (278 l), `engine/math/arc_interpolation.py` |
+| 2 | **2D viewer + blueprint renderer** — per-face viewports (v/o/u/h), all-mode 2×2 grid, unfold with bands/title-block/cartouche, auto-dims, miter angles, grid, break-lines, measurements | `ui/qt_viewer.py` (1448 l), `engine/render_2d/renderer_2d.py` (2041 l) |
+| 3 | **3D viewer** — arcball rotate, target orbit, wireframe/section/spin, raycast hole picking, measure + OSNAP glyphs, palette | `ui/qt_viewer_3d.py` (1418 l), `core/part3d.py` (982 l) |
+| 4 | **OSNAP engine** — snap math isolated in pure-geometry leaf, design-layer facade, drives 2D/3D/blueprint/measure toolbar | `engine/math/osnap.py` (422 l), `design/snaps.py` facade |
+| 5 | **Metrology** — corner angles with verdicts, distance/angle labels, measure toolbar (major/minor axis, drafting settings dialog) | `design/measure.py`, `ui/toolbars/measure_toolbar.py`, `ui/dialogs/drafting_settings.py` |
