+
+## 3. ARCHITECTURAL WEAKNESSES (Spaghetti Code & Poor API)
+
+### 3.1 SOLID violations — evidence
+- **SRP / Monolith:** `ui/app.py` = **5810 lines, 249 methods** — 2.8× larger than the next-largest file. One class owns: startup/bootloader, imports (NC1/DXF/DWG/folder/projects), the file table + editable delegates, hole editing + undo/redo, measurement, view options, settings (5 nested dialog builders: `make_lang/make_theme/make_columns/make_output/make_si/make_affich` inside `_open_settings`), organize popup, export, order management, project persistence, close-confirmation. This class will not "collapse"; it already exceeds what one human can fully review — 249 methods is beyond testable reasoning.
+- **UI ↔ parsing coupling (violates Clean Architecture):** `app.py` calls `parse_geometry`/`apply_edits`/`apply_hole_edits`/`(part3d) profile_info` directly and *inside* dozens of methods with inline `from ... import` (2659, 2618, 2626, 2833...). There is no application/service boundary between the UI and the geometry engine; the geometry dict contract is the only seam. Refactor target: a `HoleEditService`/`GeometryService` the UI calls.
+- **Layer inversion:** `engine/render_2d/renderer_2d.py` (engine layer) imports `nccorrection.ui.components.scaling` (`sp`) and `nccorrection.design.*` — the "engine" depends on UI and on a *second* design package that parallels `ui/styles.py`.
+- **Two design systems:** `design/` (theme/snaps/measure/glyphs — the viewers' palettes) coexists with `ui/styles.py` (global QSS theme: `apply_theme`, `THEMES`, `shade` — `app.py:36`). Both are live (§1), but color/dimension authority is split across two layers with no documented precedence.
+- **OCP:** the BO feature-shape table is string-tolerance in one regex (`BO_TOKEN`) — works, but adding a DSTV shape variant (e.g. new marker letters) means editing the parser rather than registering a rule.
+- **DIP:** `app.py:33` `QMessageBox` popups — 33 usages in app.py + 2 in `create_file_dialog.py` — hard-wired modal dependencies directly in the main class; also clashes with the owner's "no pop-ups" doctrine (C2 applied it only to `profile_builder.py`, which is unreachable anyway — see §4).
+
+### 3.2 Duplicated / parallel implementations (registered, not exhaustive)
+- **BO parse logic:** canonicalized in C2 into `core/viewer.parse_bo_feature` (good), but `nc1_writer._format_feature`/`apply_hole_edits` re-implements the same shape table for writing (`len(nums)>=6 / len(nums)>3` branches at `nc1_writer.py:98-106`) — read/write risk of drift.
+- **Face-rule tables:** `face_planes.real_faces`, `nc1_writer.valid_faces`, `coordinate_transform` docstrings "mirror" each other (acknowledged in comments, still three sources).
+- **`_loop_inside`/`_polygon_centroid`/`_point_in_polygon`** in `dxf_parser.py` (235-266) vs geometry primitives in `part3d.py` — pure-geometry helpers exist in two engine modules with no shared `engine/math/geom.py`.
+
+### 3.3 Testability
+- Inline closures in `_edit_hole_dialog` (`_parse`, `make_edit`, `y_mode`, `collect`, `rebuild_preview`, `on_y_changed`, `on_mode_changed`, `on_face_changed`, `on_axis_clicked`, `reset_fields`) and `_open_settings` (6 `make_*`) — logic embedded in dialog closures, untestable without instantiating the whole `NCManagerApp`.
+- `tests/test_ui.py` (2196 l) couples UI tests to internal attribute names — brittle by design (documented flaky `test_ask_save_copy` / `test_animated_button_hover_animates`).
+
