+## Decisions Log (continued — NC1 RADIUS CONVENTION, 2026-09-14)
+
+- **NC1 RADIUS CONVENTION SUPPORT IMPLEMENTED (owner directive: "Focus into our engine to make it more flexible. Download an open source one and read the code and focus to make our engine the same — can read all NC1 files"). Verified by guardian 2026-09-14: 827 ran / 823 OK (same 3+1 pre-existing failures). No regression. Smoke PASS.**
+
+  **Problem:** The 3rd column of AK/IK contour lines in NC1/DSTV files is ambiguous in the wild. The DSTV standard says it's `bulge = tan(θ/4)` (always in [−1, +1]), but some CAM post-processors (Lantek, ProNest) write `radius` in mm (can exceed 1.0). Our engine treated it as bulge, producing absurd 38-meter arcs for circular plates like T10.nc1 (PL20, Ø544.6mm).
+
+  **Open-source reference:** `tluijken/dstv` (Rust, MIT, 3★) and `Baseflow/DSTV.Net` (C#, MIT, 8★) both call the 3rd column `radius` and render via SVG arc commands.
+
+  **Detection rule:** If ANY vertex in a contour has `|3rd_column| > 1.0` → radius convention (impossible for bulge, since `tan(θ/4) ≤ 1.0` for arcs ≤ 180°). Otherwise → bulge convention (backward compat).
+
+  **Files changed (6 surgical edits):**
+  1. `engine/parser/dstv_part.py` — Added `radius: float = 0.0` field to `DstvVertex`
+  2. `engine/parser/dstv_parser.py` — Added `_classify_arc_convention()` function (detection + bulge→radius conversion); wired into `parse_text()` after contour assembly
+  3. `engine/math/arc_interpolation.py` — Added `radius_to_arc_points()` function + `_circle_from_points()` optimisation for single-radius contours; updated `polyline_for_vertices()` to accept 4-tuples `(x, y, bulge, radius)` with radius priority
+  4. `engine/render_2d/renderer_2d.py` — Updated `_face_geometry()` to pass `(v.x, v.y, v.bulge, v.radius)` 4-tuples
+  5. `core/viewer.py` — Updated `parse_geometry()` to store 3rd column in `contour_meta['arc_values']` + detect `arc_convention` per contour
+  6. `ui/qt_viewer.py` — Updated `_draw_shapes()` to use `polyline_for_vertices` arc interpolation when `contour_meta` has arc data
+
+  **Files NOT touched:** `app.py`, `part3d.py`, `fold.py`, `hole_ops.py`, `dxf_writer.py`, `format_analyzer.py`, `classifier.py`
