+## Decisions Log (continued — CONTOUR ENGINE PHASE 1 IMPLEMENTATION, 2026-09-16)
+
+- **CONTOUR ENGINE PHASE 1 IMPLEMENTED: 6 modules in `engine/contour/`, 33 tests, all PASS. Full suite 1127/1127 OK. Zero regressions.**
+
+  **Owner directive (2026-09-16):** Build an algorithmic Contour Engine that generates correct AK face geometry for ANY profile (I, U, L, B, O, T) with ANY cut angle combination — no templates. Owner provided 3 critical corrections: (1) `dims[8]/dims[9]` header order varies by profile kind — use flexible parser; (2) IK = independent contour (clockwise, boolean subtraction); (3) KA col6 = radius/k-factor, thickness from header. Option A (Sequential Pipeline) confirmed as the correct approach.
+
+  **Architecture (6 modules, each <200 lines):**
+  ```
+  engine/contour/
+  ├── __init__.py              ← Pipeline orchestrator + generate_nc1() API
+  ├── profile_model.py         ← ProfileGeometryModel data layer
+  ├── cut_interpreter.py       ← Cut angle math (web_offset = H×tan(θ))
+  ├── notch_detector.py        ← w/t suffix detection from AK blocks
+  ├── contour_builder.py       ← Final AK point assembly per face
+  └── nc1_writer_advanced.py   ← NC1 text output with correct suffixes
+  ```
+
+  **Key design decisions:**
+  - `ProfileGeometryModel.from_header(dims, kind_code)` — flexible parser that reads cut angles based on profile kind (I/U get 4 angles, L/B/O/T get none)
+  - Face mapping: I/U → v(web=H), o(flange=b), u(flange=b); L → v(leg1=H), u(leg2=b); B → v(width=depth)
+  - Plate face width uses `model.depth` (dims[1] = stocked width), NOT `model.width` (dims[2] = thickness)
+  - Cut angles use 3 decimal places in ST header (matching template ground truth)
+  - Suffix semantics: s=Start, u=Continuation, w=Hole/Notch, t=Tangential Notch
+
+  **Ground truth verification against 37 NC1 templates:**
+  - 32 simple templates (86%): all produce rectangular 5-point faces ✓
