+## 4. Recommended Architecture for NC Manager Cotation Engine
+
+### 4.1 Data Model (extend `design/measure.py`)
+
+```python
+@dataclass
+class DimensionPoint:
+    """A single measurement point projected onto a direction line."""
+    world: Tuple[float, float]      # original world position
+    projected: float                 # distance along direction line from origin
+    label: str = ""                  # optional override label
+
+@dataclass
+class DimensionSet:
+    """A chain of measurements along a reference direction."""
+    ref_p1: Tuple[float, float]     # reference line start
+    ref_p2: Tuple[float, float]     # reference line end
+    points: List[DimensionPoint]    # measurement points (in chain order)
+    offset: float = 30.0            # distance of dimension line from part (mm)
+    kind: str = "linear"            # linear | perpendicular | parallel | free | angular | arc
+    style: 'DimensionStyle' = None  # visual style
+
+@dataclass
+class DimensionStyle:
+    text_height: float = 3.5        # mm
+    arrow_size: float = 2.5         # mm
+    precision: int = 0              # decimal places
+    extension_gap: float = 1.5      # gap between part and extension line start
+    line_offset: float = 0.3        # dimension line thickness
+```
+
+### 4.2 Engine Module Structure
+
+```
+engine/cotation/
+├── __init__.py
+├── models.py          # DimensionPoint, DimensionSet, DimensionStyle
+├── linear.py          # horizontal, vertical, orthogonal dimensions
+├── aligned.py         # perpendicular, parallel, free dimensions
+├── angular.py         # angular + arc dimensions
+├── chain.py           # add/remove points, link/unlink chains
+├── auto_dim.py        # grid-based auto-dimensioning
+└── renderer.py        # QPainter rendering of dimension sets
+```
+
+### 4.3 Rendering Rules (from Tekla screenshots)
+
+**Linear dimension appearance:**
+```
+     ← 80 → ← 80 →
+     |       |       |
+─────┼───────┼───────┼─────  ← dimension line
+     |       |       |
+     ← extension lines extend from part edges
+```
+
