+# NC Manager V1.21 UI System Redesign Contract
+
+## Purpose
+This document records the updated professional UI contract requested by the user. OpenCode must implement these requirements in the real Python/Tkinter desktop app without redesigning, simplifying, or creating duplicate apps.
+
+## Active UI Source
+
+```text
+Nc corection/NC manager v1.20 PLANNING/ui/NC_MANAGER_UI_ACTIVE.html
+```
+
+The active UI file is the visual and behavior contract.
+
+## Core Direction
+The application must be one protected, expandable NC Manager V1.21 system, not a superficial demo. The UI must be separated into clear areas so the program can evolve, be packaged, and potentially become closed-source later.
+
+## 1. Settings System
+Settings must not be rough tab buttons. Settings must be a professional navigation system:
+
+- Left-side settings menu/list.
+- Clicking one setting category opens its own settings page.
+- Settings categories currently required:
+  - General
+  - Project Save
+  - Paths / Output
+  - Table Columns
+  - Layout Profiles
+  - Operations
+  - Theme Builder
+  - Audit / History
+  - Protection
+  - Shortcuts
+  - Help
+
+Settings must persist project-wide where applicable.
+
+## 2. Layout Architecture
+Layout must be customizable and separate from business logic:
+
+- User can show/hide classification panel.
+- User can show/hide 2D viewer/details.
+- User can show/hide audit/history panel.
+- User can show/hide NC1 text preview area.
+- User can restore `Default Layout`.
+- Future desktop implementation must support user layout profiles so another operator can use a different comfortable layout.
+
+## 3. Operations Stage
+Operations must not be scattered in the table. They must live in a separate professional window/stage:
+
+- Button: `Operations Stage`
+- Modal/window title: `Operations Stage`
+- Stages:
+  - Intake
+  - Organize
+  - Rename
+  - NC1 Edit
+  - SI / EN
+  - O-Plane
+  - Holes
+  - Dry Run
+  - Execute
+
+The user workflow:
+1. User enters app.
+2. User can add files / scan folder.
+3. User decides later whether to organize files, rename, or edit NC1.
+4. Destructive actions require dry-run, backup, conflict check, and explicit execute confirmation.
+
+## 4. File Intake
+UI must allow both:
+
+- Browse folder.
+- Add individual files.
+- Scan folder path in the desktop app.
+
+Scan must not move/copy/edit files automatically.
+
+## 5. Table Default Columns
+The first UI must not show every column at once. Default visible important columns:
+
+- File Name
+- Path
+- Type
+- Family
+- Status
+
+Other columns must stay available in Settings > Table Columns:
+
+- Select
+- Profile
+- Qty
+- Target Folder
+- Warnings
+- Size
+- Modified
+- Hash
+- O-Plane
+- SI/EN
+- Notes
+
+## 6. Audit / History Panel
+Audit must be professional and controllable:
+
+- Good actions show OK status/code.
+- Problems show warning/error code.
+- User can delete history.
+- User can disable/enable audit.
+- User can export a report.
+- Audit/history must persist in the real desktop app.
+
+Examples:
+
+```text
+OK-101  scanned files successfully
+WRN-210 duplicate/conflict warning
+ERR-301 dry-run blocked by conflicts
+```
+
+## 7. Theme Builder
+Theme must be customizable, not just three fixed themes:
+
+- Accent color picker.
+- Contrast slider.
+- Top bar gradient start color.
+- Top bar gradient end color.
+- Settings persisted project-wide/user-wide.
+
+## 8. Output Path
+Output behavior must support:
+
+- Organize in the same folder/source structure.
+- Choose another output folder.
+- Rename output folder from `output` to any name.
+- Never create empty folders.
+
+## 9. Project Save / Reports
+Project save must cover the complete working state:
+
+- UI settings.
+- Layout profile.
+- Table columns.
+- Paths/output options.
+- Notes.
+- Audit/history.
+- Operation manifests.
+- Reports.
+
+User must be able to export report of what happened.
+
+## 10. NC1 Quantities
+The app must eventually parse quantity from NC1 content where available. The UI already has `Qty` as an available hidden column.
+
+## 11. Holes / Geometry Editing
+The UI must support a future Holes stage:
+
+- Resize holes larger/smaller.
+- Apply only to draft after parser validation.
+- Must not directly modify NC1 without dry-run/backup/execute.
+
+## 12. Removed Rough UI Elements
+The UI must not show:
+
+- `Hold click to pan` button.
+- Demo/browser/simulation wording.
+- Help/About wording.
+- Too many table columns by default.
+- Operations scattered under the file table.
+
+## 13. Icons / Attachments Binding
+All mandatory image icons are in:
+
+```text
+rsc/icons/
+```
+
+Mandatory icons:
+
+- `artsbuilderexecute.png` for app/logo.
+- `folder-cyan-open.png` for Browse.
+- `help-browser-2.png` for Help.
+
+The desktop app must load icons through a resource/icon service instead of hardcoded scattered paths where possible.
+
+## 14. Protection / Expandability
+The desktop architecture must separate:
+
+- UI layout.
+- Settings storage.
+- Icon/resource binding.
+- Project/profile storage.
+- Audit/history.
+- Operations command engine.
+- NC1 parser/classifier.
+- 2D viewer/geometry.
+- Reports/export.
+
+This separation is required so the app can expand professionally and can later be packaged or closed-source.
+
+---
+
+# Line-by-Line Correction Addendum — 2026-07-29
+
+## Required UI corrections now active
+
+1. `Add Files` must not be a text button.
+   - Use a professional file icon button.
+   - Keep Browse using `folder-cyan-open.png`.
+
+2. Remove the `Directory` label from the path bar.
+
+3. Remove all `min` buttons. If minimize/collapse is needed later, use a clear professional collapse system with documented behavior.
+
+4. Audit/History:
+   - Keep one clear `Audit / History` panel only.
+   - Do not show fake startup success entries.
+   - Audit entries appear only after real user action or real validation.
+   - `Delete history`, `Disable audit`, and `Export report` must be inside a dropdown menu.
+
+5. Operations:
+   - Do not duplicate Operations buttons.
+   - Open operations from clear workflow buttons only.
+   - `Sort into folders` is the clear main organize workflow button.
+
+6. Folder scan:
+   - Rename `Recursive` to `Include subfolders`.
+   - Explain it as: include files inside subfolders when scanning a folder.
+   - Rename `Scan` to `Scan folder`.
+
+7. Sorting / duplicate protection:
+   - `Sort into folders` must not duplicate work.
+   - Re-loading the same files must skip existing files instead of adding duplicates.
+   - Sorting must be blocked if conflicts exist.
+   - Sorting must be a safe plan first, not immediate destructive file movement.
+
+8. Application close:
+   - Program close X must open confirmation modal.
+   - Modal must show warning symbol.
+   - Buttons required:
+     - Save
+     - Cancel
+     - Close
+
+9. Undo / Redo:
+   - Add Undo and Redo buttons.
+   - They must be disabled when no action is available.
+   - They must restore relevant UI/project state where supported.
+
+10. Theme:
+   - Use page name `Theme`, not `Theme Builder`.
+   - Show ready themes first:
+     - Industrial Dark
+     - Steel Blue
+     - High Contrast
+   - Show advanced controls only after pressing `Customize`.
+
+11. Help:
+   - Settings > Help must show Help content directly.
+   - Do not require another click on a Help icon/button to show information.
+
+12. Buttons:
+   - Visible buttons must either perform their action or show a truthful safe-block/status message.
+   - No fake pass, fake report, or fake audit result.
+
+---
