+# NC Manager V1.21 Icons Manifest
+
+## Active image icons
+
+| File | Purpose | Source | Status | Where used |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `artsbuilderexecute.png` | Main NC Manager V1.21 app/logo | User-provided file | Active / mandatory | Header brand/logo, desktop app icon candidate |
+| `folder-cyan-open.png` | Add NC/NC1 files icon | User-provided file | Active / mandatory | Path bar `Add NC/NC1 files` icon button |
+| `help-browser-2.png` | Help icon | User-provided file | Active / mandatory | Settings > Help and Help modal |
+
+## Active inline UI control icons
+
+These are embedded as inline SVG or styled control glyphs inside the active UI preview, not separate image files. They are allowed only for generic controls that do not have user-provided PNG files yet.
+
+| Inline/control icon | Purpose | Source/license | Where used |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `settings` | Open Settings menu | Arena-authored inline SVG, no external download | Header Settings button |
+| `close-x` / `×` | Close drawer, close modals, close application request | Standard UI glyph, no external download | Settings, Help, Operations Stage, app close |
+| `status-ok` / `✓` | Audit OK status | Standard UI glyph, no external download | Audit / History panel |
+| `status-warn` / `⚠` | Audit warning status | Standard UI glyph, no external download | Audit / History panel |
+| `status-error` / `✖` | Audit error status | Standard UI glyph, no external download | Audit / History panel |
+
+## Current path-bar decision
+
+The separate `Browse` button is removed by user request.
+
+Current path bar must keep:
+- path entry
+- `Add NC/NC1 files` icon button using `folder-cyan-open.png`
+- `Scan folder`
+- `Sort into folders`
+- `Include subfolders`
+
+## Binding rule for desktop implementation
+
+The real Python/Tkinter app must not scatter hardcoded icon paths across random UI files.
+
+Implement an icon/resource binding layer where practical, for example:
+
+```text
+src/nccorrection/ui/icon_factory.py
+src/nccorrection/services/resource_service.py
+```
+
+Required behavior:
+- load icons from `rsc/icons/`
+- validate mandatory icons at startup/smoke test
+- fail/report clearly if mandatory icon is missing
+- document every new icon in this manifest
+
+## Mandatory production image icon path
+
+```text
+rsc/icons/
+```
+
+## Tracking rule
+Each production image icon must track:
+- filename
+- purpose
+- source
+- license/owner note
+- where used
+
+Inline/glyph controls must stay documented here and must not replace the three mandatory user-provided PNG icons.
