+# DSTV ENGINE FIX REPORT
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-03
+**Prompt:** PROMPT 10 — Fix and build the DSTV NC1 2D/3D rendering engine
+**Project root:** `C:\Users\ouahb\Desktop\NCCORECTION v1.10_UI_IMPL_WORKING_COPY`
+
+---
+
+## FILES_READ
+
+- `src/nccorrection/core/viewer.py` — existing `parse_geometry` / `AKTOK` / `classify_cuts` (reference for the real DSTV AK 7-column layout and dims ordering)
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/app.py` — main window (`NCManagerApp`), viewer control bar and `view_stack`
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer.py` — existing Qt 2D viewer (`NcViewer`)
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer_3d.py` — existing Qt 3D viewer (`NcViewer3D`), rotation matrix convention reused
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/translations.py` — translation keys (EN/FR)
+- `tests/test_ui.py`, `tests/test_part3d.py` — existing test conventions (unittest + `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`)
+- Real `.nc1` fixtures under `projects/01-CN/input/` (IPE360 / PL profiles) used to validate the parser
+
+## FILES_CREATED
+
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/__init__.py`
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/dstv_part.py` — `DstvVertex`, `DstvContour`, `DstvHole`, `DstvMarking`, `DstvHeader`, `DstvPart`
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/dstv_face.py` — `DstvFace` (per-face container: outer contour, inner contours, holes, markings)
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/dstv_parser.py` — `DstvParser` (`parse_file`, `parse_text`, `_parse_st_block`, `_parse_bo_block`, `_parse_ak/ik`, `_parse_marking_line`)
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/arc_interpolation.py` — `bulge_to_arc_points`, `polyline_for_vertices`
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/coordinate_transform.py` — `FaceCoordinateSystem` (bounds per face + Y inversion)
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/renderer_2d.py` — `DstvRenderer2D` (Qt face-by-face view + 2x2 all-faces grid)
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/renderer_3d.py` — `DstvRenderer3D` (Qt isometric wireframe, drag-rotate/pan, presets)
+- `tests/test_dstv_engine.py` — 16 tests
+
+## FILES_MODIFIED
+
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/app.py`
+  - Imported `DstvParser` + `DstvRenderer2D`.
+  - Added `self.face_viewer = DstvRenderer2D` as a third page in `view_stack` (`2D` / `Faces` / `3D`).
+  - Added a face selector group in the 2D control bar: `ALL | V | O | U | H` (exclusive `QButtonGroup`).
+  - Extended `_view_mode` with the `'faces'` state; updated `_set_view_mode`, `_toggle_view_mode`, `_viewer_fit`, `_viewer_zoom`, `_screenshot`, `_viewer_menu`, `_apply_view_opt('2d_grid')`.
+  - Added `_select_face(code)` which parses the current file with `DstvParser` and drives the face viewer.
+  - Fed/cleared the face viewer from `_refresh_viewers` and the `_update_details` empty-selection branch.
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/translations.py`
+  - Added keys `faces` and `face_hint` (EN + FR).
+
+## FILES_DELETED
+
+- None.
+
+## SUMMARY_FILE_CHANGE_DETAILS
+
+| File | Change |
+|------|--------|
+| `engine/dstv_part.py` | Data model: vertex (X, Y, bulge + optional α/β/suffix), contour (outer/inner), hole (round/slot), marking, ST header, part with per-face index. |
+| `engine/dstv_face.py` | One face = outer contour + inner contours + holes + markings, with a `bounds` property. |
+| `engine/dstv_parser.py` | Block parser. AK/IK lines are accumulated per face across lines (one 7-column vertex per line, as in real DSTV); classic `X Y bulge` triples are also supported. BO handles plain + slotted holes. SI/PU/KO produce markings. Numbers are matched with a look-behind so piece marks like `SAMPLE-1` are preserved. |
+| `engine/arc_interpolation.py` | `bulge = tan(θ/4)` → arc centre/radius/sweep; direction chosen so the arc apex sits on the correct side of the chord (left for bulge>0). |
+| `engine/coordinate_transform.py` | Per-face bounds (v/h: length×height; o/u: length×width; B: length×width) and the mandatory Y inversion `canvas_y = height − y·scale − offset`. |
+| `engine/renderer_2d.py` | Qt widget. Renders the active face (grid, outer contour with arcs, IK cut-outs filled, BO circles + crosshair + Ø label, SI/PU/KO markings, bounds readout) or all faces in a 2x2 grid with per-quadrant auto-fit. Wheel zoom + middle-drag pan. |
+| `engine/renderer_3d.py` | Qt widget. Places each face in 3D (v in x-z, h mirrored, o/u on flange planes), orthographic rotation (drag), wheel zoom, axes + per-face legend, presets (iso/top/front/right). |
+| `ui/app.py` | Wiring above. No existing button/feature was removed; the 2D/3D toggle semantics are preserved. |
+| `ui/translations.py` | `faces`, `face_hint` keys. |
+| `tests/test_dstv_engine.py` | 16 tests (see below). |
+
+## SUMMARY_TEST_DETAILS
+
+`PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -q`
+
+- Before: 150 tests OK.
+- After: **166 tests OK** (150 existing + 16 new, none broken).
+
+New tests (`tests/test_dstv_engine.py`):
+
+1. `test_parse_st_block` — steel grade, quantity, profile type/name, all dims.
+2. `test_parse_bo_block` — hole positions/diameters.
+3. `test_face_filtering` — holes split by face code.
+4. `test_parse_ak_block` — 7-column vertices accumulated per face.
+5. `test_contour_closure` — polyline closes back to the first vertex.
+6. `test_suffix_stripping` — `0.00u` / `0.00o` suffixes parsed and recorded.
+7. `test_parse_ik_block` — inner contour cut-outs.
+8. `test_si_block` — SI marking text preserved.
+9. `test_bulge_to_arc_points_zero` — straight segment = 2 points.
+10. `test_bulge_to_arc_points_semicircle` — bulge=1.0 → semicircle apex at +5.
+11. `test_bulge_negative_side` — bulge=−1.0 → apex at −5.
+12. `test_arc_parsed_from_nc1` — bulge from a real NC1 parsed & interpolated.
+13. `test_y_inversion` — DSTV Y up / canvas Y down.
+14. `test_face_bounds` — per-face (width, height).
+15. `test_valid_faces` — allowed faces per profile type.
+16. `test_full_nc1_file` — parses a real `.nc1` fixture from `projects/`.
+
+Offscreen smoke checks (not in the suite): `DstvRenderer2D` and `DstvRenderer3D` render real parts to PNG with content; `NCManagerApp` loads a file, enters `faces` mode, switches faces and toggles 2D/3D without errors.
+
+## DEVIATIONS_FROM_PROMPT
+
+- **GUI toolkit:** the prompt specified a Tkinter `Canvas`. This application is a PySide6/Qt app, so `renderer_2d`/`renderer_3d` are implemented as Qt `QWidget`s (same face-by-face logic and the same Y-inversion rule). No extra dependency was added; `PySide6` was already the project's GUI stack.
+- **Main-window file name:** the prompt said `ui/main_window.py`; the real file is `ui/app.py` (`NCManagerApp`), which is where the wiring was added.
+- **Report path:** `Nc corection/NC manager v1.20 PLANNING/reports/` does not exist in this project; reports live in `reports/`, so the report was written to `reports/DSTV_ENGINE_FIX_REPORT.md`.
+- **Test runner:** the project uses `unittest` (`discover`), so the tests are `unittest.TestCase` classes (they also run under pytest).
+- **ST header layout:** the prompt described a fixed line layout; real NC1 files use comments (`**`) and the dims start *after* the profile-type code line. The parser resolves fields heuristically (grade regex, nearest preceding name line, quantity = first integer after the grade, dims after the type line) and validates against real fixtures.
+- **Counterbores:** BO pairing at identical positions is parsed as separate holes; automatic counterbore grouping is left as a remaining improvement (does not affect rendering correctness).
+
+## REMAINING_ISSUES
+
+- Multiple inner (IK) contours on the *same* face are only separated when a contour closes onto its first vertex mid-stream; a face with several IK cutouts written without an explicit closing repeat may be merged. Works for current fixtures.
+- `DstvRenderer2D`/`DstvRenderer3D` are read-only development views; they do not reflect live hole edits from the editing panel (the main `NcViewer` still does).
+- The 3D face placement is a schematic development (web in x-z, flanges on ±H/2 planes); it is not the physical 3D part model produced by `core/part3d.py`. Use `NcViewer3D` for the real solid model.
+
+## FINAL_VERDICT
+
+**PASS** — the engine module was created and integrated, all 11 required test scenarios pass (16 assertions groups), the full suite is green (166/166), and the app starts, loads a real NC1 file, renders each DSTV face in its own viewport (with arcs, holes, IK cut-outs and markings) plus an isometric 3D wireframe, all without removing any existing functionality.
