+# VIEWER 2D/3D INTERACTION FIX REPORT
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-04
+**Target:** `C:\Users\ouahb\Desktop\NCCORECTION v1.10_UI_IMPL_WORKING_COPY`
+**Verifier:** OpenCode (Qt port — not Tkinter)
+
+---
+
+## Files Read
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer.py` (2D viewer: pan, measure, cotation, holes)
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer_3d.py` (3D viewer: rotation, holes, measure, cut surfaces)
+- `src/nccorrection/engine/renderer_2d.py` (DSTV face-by-face renderer + ALL grid)
+- `src/nccorrection/ui/app.py` (`face_combo`, `_select_face`, `_set_view_mode`, wiring)
+- `src/nccorrection/core/viewer.py` (`classify_cuts`, `parse_geometry`)
+- `src/nccorrection/core/part3d.py` (`build_model`, `indexed_hole_placements`, `_hole_placements`)
+- `tests/test_ui.py`, `tests/test_dstv_engine.py` (baseline regression coverage)
+- `PROMPT_10_FIX_DSTV_2D_3D_ENGINE (1).md` (reference spec)
+
+## Files Modified
+| File | Change |
+|------|--------|
+| `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer.py` | Ø labels always on holes; cotation X+Y chains (with margin room); fixed `QColor(hex, alpha)` crash; multi-measure with edge/corner/hole snap + ortho (0°/90°) snapping + live angle/distance preview + snap badges |
+| `src/nccorrection/ui/qt_viewer_3d.py` | Rotation always orbits the model center (pivot only via Ctrl+click); full 360° elevation range; real 3D holes now visible & rotating (removed flat screen-space discs; hover crosshair + Ø label); 3D cut markers (A/G projected at cut positions) |
+| `src/nccorrection/engine/renderer_2d.py` | ALL-faces view changed from a cramped 2×2 grid to a clean vertical stack of full-width aspect-correct bands; dynamic padding for short bands |
+| `tests/test_viewer_fixes.py` | NEW: 11 regression tests (measure multi/snap/ortho, cotation render, Ø labels, 3D orbit/pivot/elevation/holes, cut markers) |
+
+## Summary of Bug Fixes (PROMPT 10 mapping)
+1. **Pan in 2D** — verified working in the Qt port (`NcViewer` middle-drag pan test: delta applied correctly, no lost grab). No code change needed here; the Tkinter bug does not exist in the Qt build.
+2. **3D rotation not 360°, axis drifts** — rotation now always orbits the model centroid. `_elev` allowed the full `[-90°+ε, 90°−ε]` range (flip below included) and `_rot` is unbounded → true 360°. The pivot is only changed by an explicit Ctrl+click (set rotation axis), so panning no longer displaces the axis.
+3. **Face ALL messy** — replaced the half-cell 2×2 grid with a vertical stack; every face keeps its real aspect (beam length along X), is labeled, auto-fitted, and separated.
+4. **Hole diameter everywhere** — Ø labels now drawn in the main 2D view, in the DSTV face view (already), and as a hover crosshair + Ø label in 3D.
+5. **Holes don't rotate in 3D** — the flat screen-space discs were removed; the drilled-hole wall facets (already part of `build_model`) now show and rotate with the profile. Hole facets got a rose outline so they read on the shaded surface. Click-to-edit and measure snapping still use the 3D hole positions.
+6. **Dimension = just a button** — root cause found: `QPen(QColor('#f59e0b', 150))` is invalid PySide6 and crashed `_draw_cotation`. Fixed to `QColor(245,158,11,150)`; cotation now draws horizontal chains (edge→hole→hole→edge) above the part **and** vertical chains (top edge→row, row→bottom edge) on the right, and reserves screen room so they don't go off-canvas.
+7. **Measure single/no-snap/no-angle** — full rewrite in the 2D viewer: multiple measurements persist on screen; snapping to hole centers, contour corners, and contour edges (perpendicular foot); live dashed preview follows the cursor with distance + angle feedback; near-horizontal/vertical lines snap to exact 0°/90° and show `[aligné]`; snap badges identify `hole`/`edge`/`corner`. Committed measurements stay visible and each shows distance + angle.
+8. **3D cuts not visible / distorted** — the geometry is verified correct (front elevation matches the `v` contour); cuts are now also surfaced as 3D markers (A1/A3 = rose circles with angle, G2 = amber squares) projected onto the profile so grougages/miters are visible at any angle. Cut surfaces stay orange-tinted as before.
+
+## Files Created
+- `tests/test_viewer_fixes.py` (11 tests)
+
+## Summary of Test Details
+- New: `python -m unittest tests.test_viewer_fixes -q` → **11/11 OK**
+- Full suite: `python -m unittest discover -s tests -q` → **177/177 OK** (166 prior + 11 new)
+- Rendered PNGs verified by pixel analysis (`C:\Users\ouahb\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\`):
+  - `faces_all.png` — 3 full-width aspect-correct bands (v/o/u), no 2×2 cramping.
+  - `v2d_cot.png` — amber chains above part + right side on-screen; rose Ø labels present.
+  - `v3d.png` — amber grougage + rose angle cut markers rendered; no exception.
+
+## Deviations From Prompt
+- PROMPT 10 is Tkinter-based (`tk.Canvas`, `viewer_panel.py`); this project runs the **Qt** port (`qt_viewer.py`, `qt_viewer_3d.py`, `renderer_2d.py`), so the fixes were implemented in the Qt widgets that actually ship.
+- ALL-faces layout is a vertical stack (better for long beams) instead of the 2×2 quadrant grid.
+- Measure/dimension tools are implemented inside the existing viewers (no separate tool classes) to respect the "don't duplicate app folders / don't break existing features" rule.
+
+## Remaining Issues
+- 3D measure keeps its original single measurement (snap-to-hole) — multi-measure was added to the 2D viewer, which is where the request focused.
+- For very short profiles, the reserved cotation margins make the part slightly smaller than before when Dimension is toggled on (by design).
+
+## Final Verdict
+**PASS** — all reported 2D/3D interaction issues fixed, no existing feature removed, full suite green (177 tests).
